# Brewfile

Primary app list. Keep sections: bootstrap toolchain, cli, yazi deps, casks, mas.

```ruby
brew "gh"
cask "transmission"
# mas "Xcode", id: 497799835
```

- Prefer Homebrew over `install/custom/`. Custom scripts are only for apps with no formula/cask/mas.
- `eza` replaces deprecated `exa` (removed from Homebrew). Zsh aliases map `ls`/`ll`/`la`/`lt` → eza.
- Cursor stays as `cask "cursor"` so a clean VM gets it; Homebrew is idempotent if already installed.
- Yazi extras stay with Yazi (`ffmpeg`, `sevenzip`, `jq`, `poppler`, `fd`, `ripgrep`, `fzf`, `zoxide`, `resvg`, `imagemagick`, `font-symbols-only-nerd-font`). Do not drop them when editing Yazi.
- Comment unused `mas` lines; they need an App Store sign-in on the machine.
- After adding packages, mention `./bootstrap.sh --only brew` — do not run it unless asked.
